              { text: "My birthday is on the eighteenth of October", alt: ["my birthday is on the 18th of october"], ipa: "/maɪ ˈbɜːrθdeɪ ɪz ɒn ði ˌeɪˈtiːnθ əv ɒkˈtoʊbər/", es: "mái bérz-dei is on di ei-tíinz ov ok-tóu-ber", meaning: "Mi cumpleaños es el 18 de octubre", tip: "Para fechas completas usamos 'on + ordinal + of + mes'." },
              { text: "Yesterday was a very good day", alt: [], ipa: "/ˈjestərdeɪ wɒz ə ˈveri ɡʊd deɪ/", es: "iés-ter-dei uós a vé-ri gud déi", meaning: "Ayer fue un muy buen día", tip: "'Was' es pasado singular de 'be' ('uós')." },
              { text: "We were at a restaurant last night", alt: [], ipa: "/wiː wɜːr æt ə ˈrestrɒnt lɑːst naɪt/", es: "uí uér at a rés-tront last náit", meaning: "Estuvimos en un restaurante anoche", tip: "'Were' se usa con we, you y they ('uér')." },
              { text: "The food wasn't cheap", alt: ["the food was not cheap"], ipa: "/ðə fuːd ˈwɒznt tʃiːp/", es: "de fúud uó-sent chíip", meaning: "La comida no era barata", tip: "'Cheap' significa barato; 'expensive' es caro." },
              { text: "There weren't any cars", alt: ["there were not any cars"], ipa: "/ðer wɜːrnt ˈeni kɑːrz/", es: "der uérnt é-ni kars", meaning: "No había ningún auto", tip: "'There weren't' es el plural negativo en pasado." }
            ]
          },
          {
